ning the underlying rules, probably because they can leverage back-propagation to optimize their circuits over the desired target. In contrast, models with Hebbian plasticity are relatively weak at evolving their network weights to reach any given target. A local learning rule like Hebb\u2019s rule might be good enough for learning direct associations. However, the lack of feedback signals to prior layers makes it hard for the whole network to evolve in a coordinated fashion."
